@@ -3,3 +3,17 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "./src/index.js";
+
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer(doc, "");                           // doc itself
+```
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the referenced value. It throws `JsonPointerSyntaxError` when the
+pointer is not valid (RFC 6901 §3) and `JsonPointerResolveError` when it refers to nothing (§4): a missing
+member, an array index out of range or malformed (leading zeros, `-`), or a step through a non-container. Only own
+members are resolved, and the document is never modified. Both errors extend `JsonPointerError`.
